        "date": "2026-11-12T22:56:40Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(verify): the mid-turn overhang backstop reads the whole turn\n\nLaw (c3)'s backstop for stock hidden under a ledge asked 4 path\nstations x 5 turn fractions per band, so a holder or shank swinging\nthrough hidden stock between two samples got no SweepHit. It now asks\nover coarse swept cells of the same reachable set (#1313's hull-of-discs\ncover, sag at most 0.05 mm, at most 20 intervals), the kerf excused\nonly where the tip stands, one plane per (interval, chord run): at most\n20 distinct planes per live band per move, the old grid's budget.\n\nNew: verify::turn_hidden, Rest::hidden_in_cover, Cell::probes/floor,\npush_cells_with. Pinned by tests/midturn_hidden_backstop.rs.\n\nFixes #1316\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
